{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The Rice Cookout", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Rice It Up!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect Continuous vs. Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about an unspecified time in the past that is related to now or continues up to now. <br/>When you use the Present Perfect Continuous tense, the time when the action happened is also not important.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about:<ul><li>experience up to the present</li><li>change that has happened over time</li><li>an event or action that happened in the past that is important now</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present Perfect tense: Statements, Questions and Negatives", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">have</span>/<span class=\"italic\">had</span> + past participle (statement)<br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">have</span>/<span class=\"italic\">had</span> + <span class=\"italic\">not</span> + past participle (negative)<br/><span class=\"italic\">How long</span> + <span class=\"italic\">have</span>/<span class=\"italic\">had</span> + subject  + past participle? (question)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect Continuous<ul><li>to emphasize that action has continued without stopping until now and may still be taking place</li><li>when we can see the result of an action that happened in the recent past, now</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present Perfect Continuous tense: Statements, Questions and Negatives", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">have</span>/<span class=\"italic\">had</span> + past participle + <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>. (statement)<br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">have</span>/<span class=\"italic\">had</span> + <span class=\"italic\">not</span> + past participle + <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>. (negative)<br/><span class=\"italic\">How long</span> + <span class=\"italic\">have</span>/<span class=\"italic\">had</span> + subject  + past participle + <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>? (question)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect tense</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>It seems like we've waited for hours. </p><p>I haven't had time to have people over in the past month.</p><p>How long have you waited?</p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>I've been spending more and more time in specialty food emporiums.</p><p>I haven't been having dinner out with them though.</p><p>How long have you been collecting recipes?</p></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " <span class=\"italic\">Since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">For</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">In</span> for Duration", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you use the Present Perfect tense and the Present Perfect Continuous tense, you often use phrases or clauses for duration.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "These phrases or clauses begin with <span class=\"italic\">for</span>, <span class=\"italic\">in</span> or <span class=\"italic\">since</span>. They tell you how long someone/something has done or has been doing an action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">since</span> to begin a phrase or a clause (as a connector or as a preposition).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">for</span> and <span class=\"italic\">in</span> to begin a phrase (as a preposition).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Preposition</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"for\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"for years!<br/>for a bit now<br/>for 400 years\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since then\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in the past month<br/>in a while!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Connector</span></div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since I was a kid<br/>since I started college\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I've been collecting recipes since I was a kid.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've been into cooking in a big way since I started college.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Aunt Nelly has been encouraging me to follow this career path for years!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I haven't had an honest critique from an outsider in a while!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "specialty", "type": "name"}, {"content": "for a particular taste", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This shop sells specialty foods.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about cooking.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "emporium", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a store that sells special foods", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This emporium imports greek food.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "eye-opener", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that makes you see something in a different way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Shopping for food can be a real eye-opener!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "a bit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small amount of time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've wanted to come here for a bit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to itch", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to want to do something very badly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm itching to try this new recipe.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "outsider", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone not in the group", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A compliment from an outsider is always nice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to critique", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look at critically to assess good and bad points", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He always critiques the food when we eat in a restaurant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "pub", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a British-style bar", "type"